// lib/assert.synl
//
// Standard library: assert (Synth-OOP interface).
// 标准库：assert（Synth-OOP 接口）。
//
// Human-readable face of the assert library. Methods are given as signatures
// only; their behavior is supplied by the C++ backend in lib/cpp/assert.hpp.
// On `&assert;` the interpreter brings the native class online first, then
// interprets this file; the class is already registered, so its definition
// here is treated purely as documentation of the public shape. The `$Program`
// class, should one appear, is ignored in a library.
// assert 库面向人类的形态。方法仅以签名给出，真实行为由 lib/cpp/assert.hpp
// 的 C++ 底层提供。程序写 `&assert;` 时，解释器先上线原生类，再解释本文件；
// 该类已登记，此处定义仅作公开形态文档。库中出现 `$Program` 时忽略。
//
// Method signatures below carry their type constraints; the interpreter
// enforces them at the call boundary ("Argument type mismatch" on a wrong
// type). The authoritative enforced signature lives in lib/cpp/assert.hpp's
// make_sign; this file mirrors it.
// 下列方法签名均带类型约束；解释器在调用边界强制检查（类型不符产生
// "Argument type mismatch"）。强制检查的权威签名位于 lib/cpp/assert.hpp 的
// make_sign；本文件是其可读镜像。
//
// Usage / 用法：
//   &assert;
//   -(assert::Checker chk);
//   -(Counter c);
//   chk.has_method(c, "inc");   -> std::Boolean  (true if c.inc exists)
//   chk.has_changed(c);         -> std::Boolean  (true after c.inc.=(beh))

$Checker {
    @has_method  << [(target[std::Object], name[std::String]) ~> (result[std::Boolean]) { }];
    @has_changed << [(target[std::Object]) ~> (result[std::Boolean]) { }];
}
